<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fan Changsheng</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fan Changsheng was a Daoist master and hermit of Mount Qingcheng in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sichuan">Sichuan</a> in the late 3rd and early 4th centuries who supported the rebel <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/li-xiong">Li Xiong</a>. After Li Xiong took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chengdu">Chengdu</a> in 304 and founded the Cheng Han state, he made Fan his chancellor and granted him honorific titles and privileges for his followers. Fan's role reflected the strong presence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/way-of-the-five-pecks-of-rice">Celestial Masters</a> tradition among the refugees who founded the state.</p></div>
